    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "title: \"Compressing an experiment\"\n",
        "description: \"One pass to a compressed dataset whose size does not depend on the rows; the same fit; shards that merge.\"\n",
        "order: 2\n",
        "jupyter: python3\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "The universal model needs only one compressed row per stratum, an arm × cohort: the number of clusters $G_h$, the sum of the cluster summaries $\\sum u_a$, and the sum of their outer products $\\sum u_a u_a^\\top$ (the [conditionally sufficient statistics post](https://jeffwong.github.io/posts/conditionally_sufficient_statistics/)). The cluster summary $u_a$ holds the blocks $(S^Y, S, S^T)$ of the cluster's rows. It is built during the pass and never stored."
      ],
      "id": "d2f9063f"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import polars as pl\n",
        "\n",
        "import ume\n",
        "from ume.testing import simulate_accounts\n",
        "\n",
        "df = simulate_accounts(20_000, seed=2026)\n",
        "exp = ume.annotate(\n",
        "    df,\n",
        "    cluster=\"account\",\n",
        "    instrument=\"Z\",\n",
        "    treatment=\"T\",\n",
        "    cohort=\"day\",\n",
        "    covariates=ume.covariates(x1=2.0, x2=2.0, kids=0, device=ume.categorical(reference=\"tv\")),\n",
        ").metrics(ume.mean(\"y\", name=\"hours\"), ume.ratio(\"N\", \"D\", name=\"rebuffers_per_play\"))\n",
        "\n",
        "cd = exp.compress()\n",
        "cd"
      ],
      "id": "4007825b",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## A dictionary of sufficient statistics\n",
        "\n",
        "`cd` is a mapping from strata to compressed rows:"
      ],
      "id": "cef72be8"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "row = cd[ume.Stratum(Z=1, cohort=1)]\n",
        "row"
      ],
      "id": "d742da9b",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Its first moments are the three blocks, summed over the stratum's clusters. $S_{00}$ counts rows, and the indicator columns of a categorical hold counts by level:"
      ],
      "id": "1cd6aa34"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "row.blocks()[\"S\"]"
      ],
      "id": "dbc90481",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## The same fit\n",
        "\n",
        "Fitting the compressed data gives the fit on the rows, to rounding error:"
      ],
      "id": "5294b00f"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "fit_rows, fit_compressed = exp.fit(), cd.fit()\n",
        "{\n",
        "    \"max |Δβ|\": float(np.abs(fit_rows.beta - fit_compressed.beta).max()),\n",
        "    \"max relative |Δ cov|\": float(np.abs(fit_rows.cov - fit_compressed.cov).max() / np.abs(fit_rows.cov).max()),\n",
        "}"
      ],
      "id": "da9c6805",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "fit_compressed.effects()"
      ],
      "id": "fe500755",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Shards\n",
        "\n",
        "Compressed rows add. Each shard can be compressed separately, on a different machine, and the results summed. A streaming `Compressor` needs the reference points and levels fixed before the pass, so we take them from the design that `compress` resolved:"
      ],
      "id": "5394f59d"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "design = cd.design\n",
        "shards = [\n",
        "    ume.Compressor(design).update(df.filter(pl.col(\"account\") % 3 == k).sort(\"account\")).finish()\n",
        "    for k in range(3)\n",
        "]\n",
        "merged = shards[0] + shards[1] + shards[2]\n",
        "float(np.abs(merged.fit().beta - fit_rows.beta).max())"
      ],
      "id": "47db33d9",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Rows of a cluster must not be split across shards. Shuffle by cluster before sharding; a merge that sees the same cluster twice is refused.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Size\n",
        "\n",
        "The compressed dataset has the same size for 20,000 or 20 million accounts. It holds `len(cd)` strata with $1 + q + q^2$ numbers each, here:"
      ],
      "id": "8e2e3242"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "len(cd), cd.q, len(cd) * (1 + cd.q + cd.q**2)"
      ],
      "id": "9c46c33a",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    }
